WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.367
The soft phone is the browser phone your agents use.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:07.153
This video shows the administrator's side:

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:11.738
the Soft Phone tab, where the phone appears, the diagnostics tab, and the

00:00:11.738 --> 00:00:14.060
dial button next to phone numbers.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.944
Every agent needs the same phone:

00:00:20.944 --> 00:00:26.389
connected to the right provider, visible where they work, and set to the right country.

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:28.790
Doing it per person does not scale.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.179
The Soft Phone tab sets all of it once.

00:00:32.179 --> 00:00:37.340
A person still needs the Use the telephony soft phone permission to see the phone.

00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:46.034
Open Settings, Communication, Telephony, and choose the Soft Phone tab.

00:00:46.034 --> 00:00:50.322
Default telephony provider is the provider every call goes through.

00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:55.022
Allowed short codes lists the short numbers agents may dial, one per line,

00:00:55.022 --> 00:00:57.313
such as a carrier service number.

00:00:57.313 --> 00:01:03.011
Short numbers are refused unless they are listed, and emergency numbers can never be added.

00:01:03.514 --> 00:01:07.549
Enable the soft phone turns the phone on for authorized users.

00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:12.889
Show the soft phone on the admin dashboard puts the phone button on the admin pages.

00:01:12.889 --> 00:01:17.814
To show it on the front end, add the Soft Phone widget under Design, Widgets.

00:01:18.389 --> 00:01:22.909
Enable the diagnostics tab adds a Diagnostics tab to the phone.

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:27.559
Recent calls to display sets how many calls the Recent tab lists.

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:32.604
Default country is the country the phone's number box starts on, and it

00:01:32.604 --> 00:01:35.311
turns a national number into a full one.

00:01:35.311 --> 00:01:38.253
Accent color changes the color of the phone.

00:01:38.253 --> 00:01:41.253
Save, and the phone follows the new settings.

00:01:45.486 --> 00:01:49.577
The phone is the round button at the bottom right of an admin page.

00:01:49.577 --> 00:01:51.706
Click it to open the soft phone.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:57.359
The Keypad dials a number, and the other tabs list recent calls and voicemail.

00:01:57.359 --> 00:02:00.852
Its status shows Ready when the provider is set up.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.495
With the diagnostics tab turned on, a Diagnostics tab shows live media statistics,

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:13.301
a microphone level meter, provider warnings and an audio test, so a sound

00:02:13.301 --> 00:02:14.944
problem can be found.

00:02:14.944 --> 00:02:18.047
Turn it on to troubleshoot, then turn it off.

00:02:18.047 --> 00:02:21.880
This site has no real provider, so a call cannot connect.

00:02:26.064 --> 00:02:30.753
Wherever the soft phone is present, a phone number field gets a dial button.

00:02:30.753 --> 00:02:34.584
Type a number in a user's phone number box, and a small phone

00:02:34.584 --> 00:02:36.356
button appears beside it.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.014
Fake numbers only here.

00:02:38.492 --> 00:02:42.532
Clicking it calls that number with the soft phone, and the same button

00:02:42.532 --> 00:02:44.553
appears on contact phone fields.

00:02:44.553 --> 00:02:46.892
An agent never has to retype a number.

00:02:51.092 --> 00:02:55.182
A new site turns on the soft phone, sets the default country, and

00:02:55.182 --> 00:02:58.582
every agent sees a phone with the right country code.

00:02:59.332 --> 00:03:05.232
A help desk turns on the diagnostics tab, so agents can test their own headset first.

00:03:05.982 --> 00:03:09.914
A team that only uses admin pages shows the phone on the admin

00:03:09.914 --> 00:03:12.632
dashboard, and keeps the front end clean.

00:03:14.632 --> 00:03:20.687
Choose the provider, turn the phone on, decide where it shows, and give agents the permission.

00:03:20.687 --> 00:03:22.262
Thanks for watching.

